WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.768
Customers text the numbers of your business, and someone has to answer.

00:00:05.768 --> 00:00:09.607
The messaging inbox is where your team does it together.

00:00:09.607 --> 00:00:13.756
This video shows how the inbox is laid out, and how to claim,

00:00:13.756 --> 00:00:17.100
answer, close, favorite and start conversations.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.622
Customers text a shop, a clinic or a help desk the way they

00:00:25.622 --> 00:00:28.760
text a friend, and they expect an answer soon.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.166
If the texts go to one person's phone, they are missed when that

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:36.300
person is away, and nobody else can see what was said.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.164
In the messaging inbox, a text to a department number lands in a

00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:46.630
shared list, any agent can claim it, and the whole history stays with the conversation.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:55.465
The list on the left shows your customers, most recent first, with a

00:00:55.465 --> 00:00:57.720
badge for the unread messages.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:03.863
The conversation in the middle shows the thread, and the buttons that act on it:

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.560
claim, transfer, close and mark spam.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.767
The composer sits under the thread.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:14.920
It has the message box, the attach button and the channel the reply goes out on.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.589
The Customer card on the right shows who the customer is, and which

00:01:19.589 --> 00:01:21.790
contact records match their number.

00:01:26.014 --> 00:01:27.815
Open Messaging, Inbox.

00:01:27.815 --> 00:01:33.025
The list shows each customer once, with the newest conversation on top, and

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:36.434
a red badge with the number of unread messages.

00:01:36.897 --> 00:01:39.572
Type in Search to narrow the list.

00:01:39.572 --> 00:01:46.327
The Filter button chooses All conversations, My conversations or Unassigned, each with a count.

00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:51.830
The Available switch says whether you accept conversations that are routed to you.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.903
It matters only to queues that hand out conversations one by one.

00:01:56.373 --> 00:02:00.747
The star button shows your favorite customers, and the blue button with the

00:02:00.747 --> 00:02:02.853
pencil starts a new conversation.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.867
Click a customer to open the conversation.

00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:12.529
The chip at the top says where it sits:

00:02:12.529 --> 00:02:14.896
here, in the Support shared inbox.

00:02:15.373 --> 00:02:17.841
Click Claim to make yourself the owner.

00:02:17.841 --> 00:02:23.053
The conversation leaves the shared inbox, and no other agent can reply to it by accident.

00:02:23.526 --> 00:02:26.146
Type your reply in the message box.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:30.619
Press Enter or click the send arrow to send, and Shift and Enter

00:02:30.619 --> 00:02:32.280
to start a new line.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.626
Replying to a conversation nobody holds claims it for you too.

00:02:51.665 --> 00:02:53.836
Your message joins the thread.

00:02:53.836 --> 00:02:59.565
The delivery of a text depends on the SMS provider, which the administrator sets up once.

00:03:03.757 --> 00:03:08.791
Open another conversation and click Close when the customer has what they need.

00:03:08.791 --> 00:03:12.997
A closed conversation says it is closed and cannot be replied to.

00:03:13.471 --> 00:03:16.053
Reopen brings the conversation back.

00:03:16.053 --> 00:03:21.341
If someone writes again after you closed it, the conversation reopens by itself.

00:03:21.793 --> 00:03:26.378
Mark spam closes a conversation that is not from a real customer.

00:03:26.378 --> 00:03:30.963
Use it, rather than Close, for texts you do not want in the list.

00:03:35.169 --> 00:03:38.545
Click Add to favorites on a customer you text often.

00:03:38.545 --> 00:03:43.259
The button then reads Favorite, and clicking it again removes the customer.

00:03:43.724 --> 00:03:47.002
The star button above the list shows your favorites.

00:03:47.002 --> 00:03:51.354
They are your own, up to one hundred, and other agents do not see them.

00:03:51.835 --> 00:03:55.507
The attach button beside the channel name adds pictures.

00:03:55.507 --> 00:03:59.829
You can also drag a picture onto the conversation, or paste it into

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:02.375
the message box, up to ten at a time.

00:04:06.608 --> 00:04:11.124
The Inbox menu item shows how many conversations are waiting for you, and

00:04:11.124 --> 00:04:14.268
the Messaging icon turns red while there are any.

00:04:14.727 --> 00:04:18.826
On any other admin page, a notice pops up at the bottom right

00:04:18.826 --> 00:04:20.600
when a customer writes.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.537
Click the notice to open the conversation.

00:04:23.988 --> 00:04:27.546
The count and the notices start once you have opened the inbox for

00:04:27.546 --> 00:04:30.758
the first time, because that visit ties you to your queues.

00:04:34.961 --> 00:04:37.633
Click the pencil button to write first.

00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:41.611
From is the number you send from, and it decides the channel.

00:04:42.082 --> 00:04:46.261
In To, search for contacts or leads, or type a number.

00:04:46.261 --> 00:04:51.972
Under Other, add numbers that are not in your contacts, separated by commas.

00:04:52.442 --> 00:04:54.861
Write your message and click Send.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:05:01.272
One recipient starts a conversation, and several recipients each get their own private conversation.

00:05:05.472 --> 00:05:10.892
A repair shop tells customers when a bike is ready, and answers the question that follows.

00:05:11.642 --> 00:05:14.294
A support team shares one number.

00:05:14.294 --> 00:05:19.802
Whoever is free claims the next text, and the history helps the next agent.

00:05:20.552 --> 00:05:26.292
A sales team keeps its best customers as favorites, and starts the conversation itself.

00:05:27.042 --> 00:05:32.372
A manager opens the Unassigned view to see which texts nobody has taken yet.

00:05:34.372 --> 00:05:39.900
One shared inbox for every text a customer sends, with the history in one place.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.572
Thanks for watching.

